  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Danilo Coppola began working with his father as a teenager and inherited the family construction company in 1995. He expanded from residential development around Rome into commercial buildings, hotels and property projects in Milan. Profits were also channelled into listed shares, and he came to control almost three quarters of IPI, a major Italian real-estate company.\n\nCoppola became nationally known during the contested banking takeovers of the mid-2000s, when he held interests in BNL, Mediobanca and Antonveneta. The property group’s collapse then reshaped his public career through long-running bankruptcy cases. Extradited from Abu Dhabi in 2024 to serve a final sentence, he later moved from prison to clinical house arrest for health reasons. No continuing operating business or principal asset base is established.",
